1 NAME Charles /d'Amboise/
2 GIVN Charles
2 SURN d'Amboise
2 _MARNM d'Amboise
1 NAME Charles II d'Amboise, seigneur de Chaumont
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1473
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 FEB 1511
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://gw1.geneanet.org/frebault?lang=fr;pz=henri;nz=frebault;ocz=0;p=charles;n=d+amboise;oc=1 gw1.geneanet.org/frebault... ] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seigneur_de_Chaumont
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles d'Amboise, Seigneur de Chaumont (1473 – 11 February 1511) was a French politician and military figure, who was the French governor of Milan during the reign of Louis XII, and a French commander during the War of the League
2 CONC  of Cambrai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Chaumont-sur-Loire into the House of Amboise, Charles was the nephew of Cardinal Georges d'Amboise, prime minister of King Louis XII of France, and the son of Charles I d'Amboise, governor of Champagne and Bourgogne. He wa
2 CONC s governor of Paris, of the Duchy of Milan, of the seignory of Genoa and of the province of Normandie. In 1501 he was made French lieutenant general and then vice-roy for Lombardy, becoming a friend of Leonardo da Vinci during his
2 CONC  stay in Milan. He was Grand Master of France from 1502 to 1504 when he was made Marshal of France. From 1508 to 1510 he was also admiral of France and, in 1507, he suppressed a revolt in Genoa.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the battle of Agnadello (1509), he commanded the French vanguard. In 1510, he took command of the French forces fighting against Pope Julius II in the Romagna, for which he was excommunicated; he failed to prevent Julius from c
2 CONC apturing Bologna and Mirandola, and died of illness at Correggio during the 1511 campaign.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son George died in the Battle of Pavia (1525).
