2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Louis de Coësmes, baron de Lucé, was the son of Charles III de Coësmes, baron de Lucé, and Gabrielle d'Harcourt. He married Anne Jeanne de Pisseleu, daughter of Adrien de Pisseleu, seigneur de Heilly, and Charlotte d'Ail
2 CONC ly, daughter of Louis d'Ailly, seigneur de Varennes, and Charlotte de Bournonville. Anne Jeanne was the niece of Anne de Pisseleu, duchesse d'Etampes, half-sister of her father and mistress of François I, king of France. Louis and
2 CONC  Anne Jeanne had a son Jean, who married Françoise de Maridort but died in 1574 without progeny, and a daughter Jeanne, who inherited the lordship of Bonnétable and brought it to her marriage with Louis, comte de Montafié. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis renovated the château de Bonnétable, and founded the College de Bonnétable (a school for boys). He died in 1563.
