1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LUDOVICK STEWART Duke of Lennox===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Great Admiral and Chamberlain of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p527.htm#i5262]
2 CONT  Ludovic Stewart, 2nd Duke of Lennox was born on 29 September 1574. He was the son of Esmé Stuart, 1st Duke of Lennox and Catherine de Balsac. He married, firstly, Lady Sophia Ruthven, daughter of William Ruthven, 1st Earl of Gowr
2 CONC ie and Dorothea Stewart, before June 1590. He married, secondly, Jean Campbell, daughter of Sir Matthew Campbell and Isabel Drummond, circa August 1598.2 He married, thirdly, Frances Howard, daughter of Thomas Howard, 1st Viscount
2 CONC  Howard of Bindon and Mabel Burton, on 16 June 1621. He died on 16 February 1624 at age 49. He was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.
2 CONT      Ludovic Stewart, 2nd Duke of Lennox gained the title of Duke of Richmond. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Duke of Lennox [S., 1581] on 26 May 1583. Child of Ludovic Stewart, 2nd Duke of Lennox 1.Sir John Stuart Citations 1.[
2 CONC S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family." 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th ed
2 CONC ition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
