1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARY GORDON ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Lady Mary Gordon was the daughter of George, first Marquess of Huntly. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07paul/page/516/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 516]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07paul/page/516/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 516]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10942.htm#i109419 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Gordon [1]
2 CONT *F, #109419, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1600, 
2 CONT *d. 1674
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.49%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Gordon was born circa 1600.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of George Gordon, 1st Marquess of Huntly and Lady Henrietta Stuart.[1],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Douglas, 1st Marquess of Douglas, son of William Douglas, 10th Earl of Angus and Elizabeth Oliphant, on 15 September 1632 at Bellie, Scotland.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1674.[2] She was buried at Douglas, Scotland.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT From 15 September 1632, her married name became Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Mary Gordon and William Douglas, 1st Marquess of Douglas
2 CONT *1. Lady Henrietta Douglas+[3] b. c 1633, d. 1 Jun 1673
2 CONT *2. Lady Catherine Douglas [3] b. bt 1633 - 1641
2 CONT *3. William Douglas-Hamilton, 1st Earl of Selkirk+[1] b. 24 Dec 1634, d. 18 Apr 1694
2 CONT *4. Maj.-Gen. George Douglas, 1st Earl of Dunbarton+[3] b. 1635, d. 20 Mar 1691/92
2 CONT *5. Lady Isabel Douglas+[3] b. c Apr 1642, d. 2 Dec 1691
2 CONT *6. Lady Jean Douglas+[3] b. bt 1643 - 1655
2 CONT *7. Lady Lucy Douglas+[3] b. bt 1644 - 1654, d. 8 Jan 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VI, page 265. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume IV, page 437.
2 CONT *3. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 1282. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baroneta
2 CONC ge, 106th edition.
