1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Hamilton, 3rd Lord Hamilton, Baron of Strabane</strong> (1633 – 16 June 1655) was an Irish peer, the elder son of Claud Hamilton, 2nd Baron Hamilton of Strabane and Lady Jean Gordon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father in the peerage in 1638. A Roman Catholic, he joined Sir Phelim O'Neill and commanded the defense of Charlemont in 1650. The fortress fell to the Cromwellians in August; Hamilton became a fugitive and was ca
2 CONC ptured soon after. His lands were confiscated, and he sought the protection of Sir Charles Coote; but in December 1650, he returned to his old cause and took arms again with Sir Phelim. He died at Ballyfathen in 1655, and was succ
2 CONC eeded by his brother George."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Hamilton, 3rd Baron Hamilton of Strabane', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 22 January 2012, 15:49 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Hamilton,_3rd_Baron_Hamilto
2 CONC n_of_Strabane&oldid=472624781> [accessed 30 December 2012]
