2 DATE 23 JUL 1756
2 PLAC Paris, France
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles-Armand_de_Gontaut,_duc_de_Biron
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Armand de Gontaut, duc de Biron (1663 — 1756), great-grandson of Armand de Gontout-Biron, was a French military leader who served with distinction under Louis XIV and Louis XV, and was made a Marshal of France by the latte
2 CONC r.
2 CONT
2 CONT He commanded the French vanguard at the Battle of Oudenaarde (1708), and noticed the first manoeuvre of deviation by Marlborough. Nevertheless, opposed on his lines by numerical superior forces, he was unable to change the course 
2 CONC of events that were to happen.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Oudenarde
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie-Antoinette, duchesse de Lauzun and niece of Antoine Nompar de Caumont, duc de Lauzun.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 14 children among whom were
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louis Antoine de Gontout (1700–1788), Marshal of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Charles-Antoine (1708–1800), Duc de Biron and father of the memoirist Armand Louis de Gontaut, duc de Biron 1747-1783.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Judith-Charlotte, married 07/05/1717 Claude Alexandre de Bonneval.
2 CONT  Geneviève, married 11/03/1720 Louis duc de Gramont, son of Antoine V de Gramont.
