1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabrielle_de_Rochechouart_de_Mortemart_(nun)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Gabrielle de Rochechouart de Mortemart
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabrielle 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marchioness of Thianges 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Claude Leonor Damas de Thianges 
2 CONT
2 CONT Full name 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabrielle de Rochechouart de Mortemart 
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble family House of Damas
2 CONT
2 CONT House of Rochechouart 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Gabriel de Rochechouart de Mortemart 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Diane de Grandseigne 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1633 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 12 September 1693 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabrielle de Rochechouart de Mortemart, Marchioness of Thianges (1633 – 12 September 1693) was a French noblewoman. A great beauty and wit, she was the older sister of Françoise de Rochechouart de Mortemart, Madame de Montespan.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabrielle was the eldest child of Gabriel de Rochechouart de Mortemart and his wife, Diane de Grandseigne. She joined the court in 1651 during the Fronde. She was originally placed by her parents in the household of the young king
2 CONC , Louis XIV. Later, she joined the household of his younger brother, Philippe, duc d'Anjou. Gabrielle and the duc d'Anjou remained close friends for the rest of their lives, even after he succeeded to the duchy of Orléans and beca
2 CONC me known at court as the notoriously flamboyant homosexual, Monsieur.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1655 she married Claude Leonor Damas de Thianges, Marquis of Thianges. The couple had four children, the third of whom married and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although she may have been a mistress of Louis XIV, she never gained the power and influence over the king exercised by her younger sister, Madame de Montespan who became the king's maîtresse-en-titre in 1668. Gabrièlle was with h
2 CONC er sister during the French military tour when Madame de Montespan became Louis XIV's mistress. She was also with the court when La Montespan gave birth to her daughter by Louis XIV, Mademoiselle de Nantes, at Tournai in June 1673
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Her daughter Diane married the homosexual Philippe Jules Mancini, duc de Nevers and nephew of Cardinal Mazarin. Through Diane, Gabrielle was the grandmother of Philippe Jules François Mancini and great-grandmother of Louis Jules M
2 CONC ancini Mazarini, the prominent French diplomat and writer. She was very close to her daughter, Diane, as well as to her sister, La Montespan.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1693, roughly 60 years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also an ancestor of the present Prince of Monaco through Prince Pierre, Duke of Valentinois She was a descendant of the duchesse de Polignac.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Claude Henri Philibert Damas de Thianges, Marquis of Thianges (1663-4 January, 1708) married twice (1) Anne Claire de La Chapelle and had no issue; (2) married again to Anne Philippe de Harlay and had no issue;
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Diane Gabrielle Damas de Thianges, Duchess of Nevers (?-12 January, 1715) married Philippe Jules Mancini and had issue;
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Louise Elvide Damas de Thianges Duchess of Ognano married Luigi Sforza-Conti, Duca di Ognano & Segni on 30 October, 1678 had no issue;
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Gabrielle Damas de Thianges (?-c.1693) never married;
2 CONT
