1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER IRVINE OF DRUM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Irvine of Drum, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Irvine-11th-Laird-of-Drum/6000000017345382449?through=6000000017344969920 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f1546&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD45%2f16%2f1546&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD45/16/1546]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1647: Extract heritable bond by Alexander Irrwing of Drum to Elspeth Irrwing, his sister, on the town and lands of Hirne, in the parish of Banchorie and sheriffdom of Kincardine, in lieu of payment due to her in terms of
2 CONC  a bond of provision, dated 14 May 1647, made by their deceased father, Sir Alexander Irrwing of Drum, in favour of James, Charles and Francis, his sons, and Anna, the said Elspeth, Jean, Isobel and Margaret his daughters.  Regist
2 CONC ered B. of C. and S. 21 December 1664. (With instrument of sasine dated 9 June and recorded P.R.S. Aberdeen and Kincardine 1 July 1662.) [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f15
2 CONC 46&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD45%2f16%2f1546&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, Titles to Land, reference GD45/16/1546]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/342/mode/2up Biographical Summary] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On March 21, 1688, he was served heir to his father, Alexander Irvine of Drum, in the lands and barony of Drum, &c. He married Margaret, daughter of Forbes of Auchreddie, and died in 1619 without issue.  In him failed the male 
2 CONC line of the family from father to son. By this circumstance the succession opened to the eldest son of Alexander Irvine of Murthill, the first nominee under the entail who had dies four years before the last laird. These Irvines w
2 CONC ere descended from Gilbert Irving, fourth son of Alexander Irvine of Drum and Jane Allardes. [http://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/342/mode/2up Thanage of Fermartyn: 342]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
