1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Princess Izabela Elżbieta Czartoryska, née Countess Morsztyn (1671–1756) was a Polish noblewoman, known for her political salon and role in the Familia party. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Jan Andrzej Morsztyn and Maria Katarzyna Gordon, and married Kazimierz Czartoryski in 1693. Through her daughter Konstancja she became the grandmother of king Stanisław August Poniatowski.
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with her husband she supported Prince of Conti as a candidate to the Polish throne. In 1736 in Warsaw, she established the first political salon, where politicians met and the Familia party conferred. Women played a signific
2 CONC ant role in those meetings.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LCXB-8DN
