1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Murray</strong> (c. 1667 – 24 March 1714) was a Scottish lawyer and politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Commissioner to the Parliament of Scotland for Selkirk from 1689 to 1702 and for Selkirkshire from 1702 until the Act of Union 1707. He was one of the Scottish representatives to the first Parliament of Great Britain unti
2 CONC l he was appointed a Lord of Session as <strong>Lord Bowhill</strong> on 7 June 1707."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'John Murray, Lord Bowhill', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 7 September 2012, 20:34 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=John_Murray,_Lord_Bowhill&oldid=511275870> [accessed 
2 CONC 28 October 2012] 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 485
2 CONT * [http://www.murraysmithgenealogypage.bravehost.com/MURR.HTM Descendants of John Murray, of Bowhill]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Bowhill House  From Wikipedia,the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Bowhill House is a historic house near Bowhill at Selkirk in the  Scottish Borders area of Scotland. It is a member of the Historic Houses Association, and one of the homes of the Duke of Buccleuch. The house is protected as a Cat
2 CONC egory A listed building,
2 CONT  and the grounds are listed on the Inventory of Gardens and Designed Landscapes in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bowhill was build in 1708 by John,Lord Bowhill, His brother William Murray had bought the land earlier in 1690, In 1747 Francis Scott,2nd  Duke of Buccleuch, bought Bowhill for his son Lord Charles Scott who wanted to stand for Pa
2 CONC rliament in Roxburgh or Selkirk.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1767, Henry,the third Duke,started to plant forest in the grounds, and in 1800,the Duke Charles started to revamp what was an occasional summer house and turned into a villa with gallery hall. Walter, 5th Duke,made changes and,
2 CONC in 1831,moved the entrance from south to north.The building was finally completed in 1876 when it was 437 feet (133m) long.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bowhill House is home to part of one of the worlds greatest private art collections. In the dining room are works by Canaletto,Gainsborough, and Reynolds.
