1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James, second titular Duke of Perth</strong>, and who, but for his attainder, would have been fifth Earl of Perth, was born at Drummond in or before February 1673, and educated at the Scots College in Paris...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...he was created a Knight of the Thistle by James in 1705...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...he assumed the title of Duke of Perth on his father's death in 1716, and died at Paris 6, and was buried in the Chapel of the Scots College 9, April 1720, in his forty-sixth year. He married (contract 5 August 1706) Jean, only 
2 CONC daughter of George, first Duke of Gordon."
2 CONT
