2 CONT "<strong>Alexander, second Lord Forbes of Pitsligo</strong>, was served heir of his father, 27 April 1637, being then under age. He appears in Parliament from 1661 till 1689, in which year he was excused from attendance. He died a
2 CONC fter 7 June 1690, when his son is still styled Master, but before the November following. He married Mary, eldest daughter of James, Earl of Buchan, by whom he had issue, one son : Alexander, his heir."
