1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Hamilton of Newton</strong>, born 30 November 1680; admitted a W.S. 3 March 1707. He is mentioned in Lockhart's <em>Memoirs</em> as the person sent by the Jacobites in Scotland in 1708 to the Duke of Hamilton, then a
2 CONC t Ashton in Lancashire, with intelligence of the projected French invasion. Died at Edinburgh 25 January 1757. He married Jean, daughter of Garthshore or Garthshore, and had issue."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/48/mode/2up The Scots Peerage], Vol. II, page 49
2 CONT
2 CONT == Arms ==
2 CONT <strong>Arms</strong> recorded in Lyon Office, 1738-47 - 1 and 4 <em>Gules, a mullet argent between three cinquefoils ermine</em>. 2 and 3 <em>Gules, a man's heart proper, shadowed or, between three cinquefoils ermine, in the fess
2 CONC  point a martlet argent for difference, impaled with</em> Garthshore. CREST: <em>A dexter hand holding a sword, indented on the back like a saw proper</em>. MOTTO: <em>Fideliter</em>
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamilt00john#page/n177/mode/2up The heraldry of the Hamiltons], page 81
