1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Catharine Leslie:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p6726.htm#i67259
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharine Leslie [1]
2 CONT *F, #67259
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Apr 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharine Leslie was the daughter of Alexander Leslie, Lord Balgonie and Lady Margaret Leslie.[1],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married George Melville, 1st Earl of Melville, son of John Melville, 3rd Lord Melville of Monymaill and Anne Erskine, on 18 January 1655.[2] From 18 January 1655, her married name became Melville.[2] As a result of her marriag
2 CONC e, Catharine Leslie was styled as Countess of Melville on 8 April 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Catharine Leslie and George Melville, 1st Earl of Melville
2 CONT *1. James Melville+[2]
2 CONT *2. Alexander Melville, Lord Raith [2] b. 23 Dec 1655, d. 27 Mar 1698
2 CONT *3. Margaret Melville+[1] b. 28 Oct 1658
2 CONT *4. David Leslie, 5th Earl of Leven+[2] b. 5 May 1660, d. 6 Jun 1728
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 380. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2312. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
