1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Esther De Turck married Abraham Bertolet  in 1735 in Oley, PA.  Esther was born in Oley, PA on September 29, 1711. She was the daughter of Issac De Turck.  Issac's sister, Ester, sold Abraham a farm in Oley townsh
2 CONC ip total ing 138 acres.  The farm was on a good site containing many fine acres of land, a lovely running stream and a fine site for the manor house which he built in 1736.  It was a substantial structure of stone, two stories hig
2 CONC h and was followed by the larger dwelling immediately adjoining in 1772 built by his son Daniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham and Esther had six children: Maria born in 1736, Daniel in 1741, Elizabeth in 1742, Samuel in 1743, Esther in 1746 and John born in 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT ******* Birth: 	Aug. 30, 1711 New York, USA Death: 	May 19, 1798 Oley Berks County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Abraham Bertolet, daughter of Isaac DeTurk and Maria DeHarcourt. Mother of Maria m Daniel Hoch, Daniel, Elizabeth m John DeTurk, Samuel, Esther m George Yoder, and John Bertolet. She was born in the Palantine camp in Schoh
2 CONC arie NY, baptized at the French church in New York City. Her baptism in French: "Baterne, amourdhuy dimance 29c d'Avril 1712, Monsieur Louis Rou, ministere, batise Esthe le Turque, nee le 30c d'Aoust dernier, fille de Isaac le Tur
2 CONC que et Maria sa femme, presente au St. Bateme par Francois Lucas at la mere du sit enfant pareetin et Matienne. L. Rou, Pasteur." (born Aug 30 1711, bp 4/29/1712) 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Reading Times 3/20/1876 Esther DeTurk Bertolet remained a widow for thirty-two years, and died in 1798, aged 88 years. She was an estimable Christian woman, and a daughter of a certain widow named Wammerin [sic widow of Peter
2 CONC  Wemar/Vemar/Weimar], who emigrated in 1713 [sic 1708 with her daughter Catharina, aged 2, on the Globe with Rev. Kocherthal from the Palatinate] from England under a passport from Queen Anne. On April 30, 1767, a year after the d
2 CONC eath of her husband [Araham Bertolet], she conveyed her property to her eldest son, Daniel Bertolet, for eleven hundred pounds English money. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LCZJ-H6Q FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 17 2021, 14:34:30 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Abraham Bertolet, daughter of Isaac DeTurk and Maria DeHarcourt. Mother of Maria m Daniel Hoch, Daniel, Elizabeth m John DeTurk, Samuel, Esther m George Yoder, and John Bertolet. She was born in the Palatine camp in Schoha
2 CONC rie NY, baptized at the French church in New York City. Her baptism in French, cited in a
2 CONT footnote in Memorials of the Huguenots in America, by A Stapleton, 1901, page 62:
2 CONT Baptism at French church in NY City:
2 CONT "Baterne, amourdhuy dimanche 29c d'Avril 1712, Monsieur Louis Rou, ministere, batise Esther le Turque, nee le 30c. d'Aoust dernier, fille de Isaac le Turque et Maria sa femme, presente au St. Bateme par Francois Lucas et la mere d
2 CONC u dit enfan parein et Marienne. L. Rou, Pasteur." (born Aug 30 1711, bp 4/29/1712)
2 CONT
2 CONT It is noted the date on her tombstone does not agree with the baptismal record.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Reading Times 3/20/1876
2 CONT Esther DeTurk Bertolet remained a widow for thirty-two years, and died in 1798, aged 88 years. She was an estimable Christian woman, and a daughter of a certain widow named Wammerin [sic widow of Peter Wemar/Vemar/Weimar], who emi
2 CONC grated in 1713 [sic 1708 with her daughter Catharina, aged 2, on the Globe with Rev. Kocherthal from the Palatinate] from England under a passport from Queen Anne. On April 30, 1767, a year after the death of her husband [Abraham 
2 CONC Bertolet], she conveyed her property to her eldest son, Daniel Bertolet, for eleven hundred pounds English money.
