1 NAME Abraham /Bertolet/
2 GIVN Abraham
2 SURN Bertolet
2 _MARNM Bertolet
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 DEC 1712
2 ADDR
3 CITY Minfeld
3 STAE Rhineland-Palatinate
3 CTRY Germany
1 BURI
2 DATE JUL 1766
2 PLAC Bertolet Union Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Oley
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE JUL 1766
2 PLAC Oley Township, Berks, Pennsylvania, BCA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Farmer - 138 Acres in Oley, PA, large manor house 1736, enlarged 1772
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham was Jean Bertolet's first born son.  He was 14 when he came to America with his family.  Abraham was born in Minfeld on December 11, 1712 and he married Esther De Turck in 1735 in Oley, PA.  Esther was born
2 CONC  in Oley, PA on September 29, 1711. She was the daughter of Issac De Turck.  Issac's sister, Ester, sold Abraham a farm in Oley township total ing 138 acres.  The farm was on a good site containing many fine acres of land, a lovel
2 CONC y running stream and a fine site for the manor house which he built in 1736.  It was a substantial structure of stone, two stories high and was followed by the larger dwelling immediately adjoining in 1772 built by his son Daniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham and Esther had six children: Maria born in 1736, Daniel in 1741, Elizabeth in 1742, Samuel in 1743, Esther in 1746 and John born in 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1726 his father, Jean Bertolet, secured a certificate of emigration showing that he was a native of Chartien Duise, in Berne Switzerland, and was then a tenant in the Convent Selt in Alsace and had permission to emigrate with h
2 CONC is wife and 5 children. This certificate was dated 4/29/1726.
