1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "In the mid 18th century ... Marie Anne Chaumont-Quitry, marquise d'Amblimont, held high positions at Versailles in the reign of Louis XV, where it was reported that she rejected the King's amorous advances out of 
2 CONC her regard for the feelings of Madame de Pompadour, who was her friend and the king's mistress ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "The families of Chaumont and Quitry had been the seigneurs de Chaumont and Quitry since the 12th century when Guillaume de Chaumont wed Isabelle, the daughter of Louis VI le Gros, king of France, and Lucienne de Rochefort.  The C
2 CONC haumont-Quitrys, as the family came to be known after a merger of the two, were among the small number of French families able to trace their nobility to the eleventh century ..." (A Lady of the High Hills: Natalie Delage Sumter B
2 CONC y Thomas Tisdale, page 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=E9oJWbRFHgsC&lpg=PA158&ots=pefHouyQMq&dq=Nathalie%20DeLage%20Sumter%20A%20Dedicated%20Life%20of%20Faith%20by%20SIster%20M.%20Ignatia%20Gavaghan%2C%20O.%20L.%20M.&pg=PA3#v=onepage&q=Beatrix&f=fal
