1 NAME James /Sutherland/ 2nd Lord Duffus
2 GIVN James
2 NSFX 2nd Lord Duffus
2 _MARNM Sutherland
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1655
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 SEP 1705
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''James Sutherland, 2nd Lord Duffus'''
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sutherland, 2nd Lord Duffus (son of Alexander Sutherland, 1st Lord Duffus) 
2 CONT
2 CONT James, second Lord Duffus, succeeded his father in 1674. He is found attending the Scots Parliament in 1678, 1681, 1685, and became a Privy Councillor in 1686. He appears to have become considerable embarrassed by debt, and is sai
2 CONC d to have sold or mortgaged his estates to his second son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1688 he was pressed for payment by one of his creditors, William Ross, younger of Kindeace, and while walking together between Balnagown and the ferry of Inverbreakie, Lord Duffus, apparently in a moment of exasperation, drew h
2 CONC is sword and ran his companion through the body. After the crime, he fled into England, where he remained until his friends procured for him a remission from the Crown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 April 1688, referring to the tragedy, his mother-in-law Lady Seaforth wrote to him, 'Many a man has fallen in such ane accident worse than your circumstances was, yet has been at peace with God and all the world, and lived ve
2 CONC ry happily for all that.'[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT His remission could not have been long delayed, as on 16 March 1689 he was one of those who subscribed the act declaring the legality of the meeting of the Estates summoned by the Prince of Orange,[2] and later, on 15 April 1690, 
2 CONC he took the oath of allegiance to the Prince as King William the Third.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1695 an Act was passed allowing him the privilege of two yearly fairs and a weekly market at Duffus.[4] In 1701 he voted on behalf of the Darien Company,[5] and he was one of those who objected to an increase of the forces.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT The second Lord Duffus died 24 September 1705, having married (contract dated 5 September 1674) Margaret, eldest daughter of Kenneth Mackenzie, third Earl of Seaforth.[7] She survived him barely a year, dying in August 1706.[8] Th
2 CONC ey had issue:--
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Kenneth, who succeeded as third Lord Duffus.
2 CONT * 2. James Dunbar of Hempriggs.
2 CONT * 3. William Sutherland of Roscommon, who took part in the rising of 1715, after which he went abroad. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (contract dated 20 and 22 October 1702) Helen, eldest daughter of William Duff of Dipple, and sister of the first Earl Fife. She died July 1740, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4. John.
2 CONT * 5. Alexander.
2 CONT * 6. Elizabeth.
2 CONT * 7. Frances.
2 CONT * 8. Henrietta, born 21 February 1684.
2 CONT * 9. Mary, married to James Sinclair of Mey, and had issue.
2 CONT * 10. Katharine, married to John Cuthbert, town-clerk of Inverness, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [1] Scottish Antiquary, iv. 51, 52. 
2 CONT * [2] Acta Parl. Scot., ix. 9. 
2 CONT * [3] Ibid., 109. 
2 CONT * [4] Ibid., 502. 
2 CONT * [5] Ibid., x. 246. 
2 CONT * [6] Ibid., 294. 
2 CONT * [7] Sutherland Book, i. 515. 
2 CONT * [8] Moray Tests. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Balfour Paul, J. (1906) The Scots Peerage, vol. 3. Edinburgh: David Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0059
2 CONT
2 CONT _______
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/10/mode/2up Page 10 No. 53
2 CONT
2 CONT (53) James, second Lord Duffus, died 24th September 1705. He was served heir to his father 10th November 1674. He married, contract dated 5th September 1674, Margaret Mackenzie, daughter of Kenneth, third Earl of Seaforth, who die
2 CONC d August 1706 leaving:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 53(a) Kenneth (No. 54).
2 CONT * 53(b) James (No. 57).
2 CONT * 53(c) William Sutherland, died s.p. Married, contract dated October 1702, Helen, daughter of William Duff of Dipple, who died July 1740.
2 CONT * 53(d) John Sutherland.
2 CONT * 53(e) Alexander Sutherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Sutherland, 2nd Lord Duffus''' (1) M, #198610, d. 24 September 1705
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sutherland, 2nd Lord Duffus married Lady Margaret Mackenzie, daughter of Kenneth Mackenzie, 3rd Earl of Seaforth and Isabel Mackenzie, circa 1674 (2).    
2 CONT * He died on 24 September 1705 (2).
2 CONT * He was the son of Sir Alexander Sutherland, 1st Lord Duffus and Margaret Stuart. (2)    
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Duffus [S., 1650] on 31 August 1674 (2).   
2 CONT * He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] in 1686 (2).   
2 CONT * He killed a creditor, William Ross, of Kindeace. He fled to England were he received immunity for the murder (2).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Sutherland, 2nd Lord Duffus and Lady Margaret Mackenzie:
2 CONT
2 CONT * William Sutherland (3);   
2 CONT * Mary Sutherland (+3);   
2 CONT * Kenneth Sutherland, 3rd Lord Duffus (+2) d. 18 Mar 1733/34;   
2 CONT * Sir James Dunbar of Hempriggs, 1st Bt. (+2)  d. 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT *[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 645. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peer
2 CONC age and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 109. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Peera
2 CONC ge.
2 CONT *[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
