1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Stewart (or Steuart) of Goodtrees</strong> of Gutteris, co. Edinburgh, 1st son and heir apparent of Sir James Steuart (or Stewart) of the same, Lord Advocate 1692-1711 (d. 1713), by his first wife Agnes, daughter of
2 CONC  the Rev. Robert Traill, was born about 1680; admitted advocate 10 June 1704; was M.P. [S] for Queensferry, 1705-07, and subsequently [G.B.] for Edinburgh, 1713-15, and was v.p.; created a Baronet [S], as above, 22 December 1705, 
2 CONC with rem. to heirs male whatsoever. He became Solicitor-General [S] in 1709. He succeeded his father in 1713, who had purchased, in 1712, the family estate of Coltness, co. Lanark, from his nephew, Sir David Steuart, 2d Baronet [S
2 CONC  1698] of Coltness. He married in 1705, Agnes, daughter of Sir Hew Dalrymple, 1st Baronet [S 1697], of North Berwick, Lord President of the Court of Session, by his first wife, Marion, daughter of Sir Robert Hamilton, one of the L
2 CONC ords of Session. He died August 1727, aged about 46. His wife survived him several years."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n453/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; page 435
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1690-1715/member/stewart-sir-james-1681-1727 The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1690-1715], ed. D. Hayton, E. Cruickshanks, S. Handley, 2002
