2 CONT ===ELIZABETH STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Stewart married Alexander Gillon of Wellhouse. The marriage was booked on 1 February 1701, at Canongate, adjacent to Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. The booking reads as follows: "Mistress Elizabeth, daughter of th
2 CONC e deceast Mr. Archibald Stewart, brother german to the E. of Murrat, and Alexander Gillon of Wellhouse, in the parish of Torpichen." [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso34scotuoft#page/508/mode/1up Parish of Holyroodhouse,
2 CONC  or Canongate. Register of Marriages, 1564-1800, p. 508]'''
2 CONT _______________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortest in-law relationship
2 CONT Elizabeth Stewart is your great aunt's first cousin 7 times removed.
2 CONT Shortest blood relationship
2 CONT Elizabeth Stewart is your fourth cousin 11 times removed.
2 CONT
