1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "VI. <strong>Roderick Mackenzie, sixth of Redcastle</strong>, usually called " Ruairi Mor," who married, first, in 1707, Margaret, daughter of Sir James Calder of Muirton, widow of Alexander Dunbar of Westfield (by whom she had se
2 CONC ven sons and a daughter), with issue — 
2 CONT * Roderick, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Colin, who in 1748, married Mary, daughter of Sir John Cochrane of Waterside, son of the Hon. Sir John Cochrane of Ochiltree, second son of the first Earl of Dundonald, with issue
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Roderick Mor had twelve other sons and two daughters, of whose history very little is known...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Roderick Mor died on the 29th of March, 1751, at Redcastle, and was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/538/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 539
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/historyofmacken00mack/page/538/mode/2up?q=536
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/historyofmacken00mack/page/540/mode/2up...
2 CONT
2 CONT "Roderick Mor had twelve other sons and two daughters, of whose history very little is known. One of the sons, '''either John or William''', married, with issue — at least two sons — the Rev. Hugh Mackenzie, who was born in 1771, 
2 CONC and was for fourteen years Baptist minister at St. Ives, where he died and was buried in 1836. Hugh married, with issue — a son and daughter, both without issue. The second son, ALEXANDER MACKENZIE, was born in 1772." 
