1 NAME George /Leslie/
2 GIVN George
2 _MARNM Leslie
1 NAME George Leslie, Sixteenth Baron of Balquhain
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 AUG 1682
2 ADDR
3 CITY Aberdeen
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 JUN 1715
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://books.google.com/books?id=lyENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA129#v=onepage&q=&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 129 - 133
2 CONT
2 CONT "George, Count Leslie,
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sixteenth Baron of Balquhain
2 CONT
2 CONT "Count George Leslie, born 26th August 1682, eldest son of Patrick, Count Leslie, fifteenth Baron of Balquhain, by his second wife, Mary Irvine of Drum succeeded as sixteenth Baron of Balquhain, on the death of his father, in 1710
2 CONC , in accordance with the agreement made with his elder brother, Count James Ernest Leslie, and in conformity with the deed of entail executed by Count Patrick Leslie in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT "From the evidence given in the law process regarding the succession to the Balquhain estates, we learn the following circumstances:-- John Steel, Mill of Fintray, deponed that when he was a servant to Count Patrick Leslie at Fett
2 CONC ernear, he heard the Count tell his company or visitors that George, his second son, had gone abroad to meet his elder brother, James Ernest, and to get from him a right to the Balquhain estates.  William Watt in Nethertown of Fet
2 CONC ternear, another witness, stated that George Leslie went abroad in 1695 to arrange with his brother the family affairs, on which occasion George Leslie had wished to go to his brother’s place of residence, but James Ernest sent hi
2 CONC m word that if he could not appear with a retinue of horse and men amounting to the value of 30,000 merks, he behoved not to come to the place of his residence in Germany; but that he, James Ernest, would meet him at Cologne, wher
2 CONC e George Leslie accordingly went, and met his brother, James Ernest, who there, by an agreement, made over to him his right of succession to the Balquhain estates.  Patrick Gordon of Aberlour, another witness, who had married Coun
2 CONC t Patrick Leslie’s youngest surviving daughter, Jean, stated that George Leslie went abroad to meet his elder brother, Count James Ernest, which he did at Cologne.  They there arranged and made a final settlement with regard to th
2 CONC e succession of the Balquhain estates, which Count James Ernest resigned in favour of his brother George, who, on his part, gave up all claim to the annual remittance which had been promised to him out of the German estates.
2 CONT
2 CONT "When Count Patrick Leslie went to reside at Fetternear, George Leslie continued to occupy the old castle of Balquhain.  We find by the Poll-books of the Shire of Aberdeen for 1696, vol. I. p. 292, that George, Count Leslie, son o
2 CONC f Patrick, Count Leslie, was residing at Balquhain with his family and servants.  After his father’s death he removed to Fetternear.
2 CONT
2 CONT "George Leslie got a charter under the Great Seal of the lands and barony of Balquhain, proceeding on the resignation of his father, Count Patrick Leslie, fifteenth Baron of Balquhain, 9th March 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT "George Leslie got a charter of the lands of Largie, proceeding on the resignation of his father, Count Patrick Leslie, 13th June 1694; sasine followed 9th July 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Leslie, schoolmaster of Chapel of Garioch, gave a receipt for £16 : 3 : 4 Scots to George Leslie of Balquhain, 2d August 1707.
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Pirie, collector of money for repairing the manse of Chapel of Garioch, gave a receipt to George Leslie of Balquhain for £33 Scots, as his proportion for the said repairs, 4th June 1709.  The Honourable Margaret Elphinstone,
2 CONC  spouse of George Leslie of Balquhain, got a charter of the lands of Tullos and an annuity of 2000 merks out of the lands of Balquhain, proceeding upon an obligation made to her by Count Patrick Leslie, father of the said George L
2 CONC eslie, 9th June 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mr. William Leslie, minister of Chapel of Garioch, gave a discharge to George Leslie of Balquhain for £23 : 2s. Scots, being his proportion for repairing the firk of Chapel of Garioch, 21st Jun 1710; also for £10 : 10s. for repai
2 CONC rs, 21st November 1712; also for £20 : 11s. for repairing the kirkyard dykes, and building a new school-house, 21st November 1712; also for the money and victual stipend for crop 1711, dated 23d January 1713; and another for crop 
2 CONC 1712, dated 6th February 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Count George Leslie married, 1706, the Honourable Margaret Elphinstone, second daughter of John, eighth Lord Elphinstone, and by her had issue --
2 CONT
2 CONT "   I. JAMES, born 25th May 1711, who succeeded as seventeenth Baron of Balquhain.
2 CONT
2 CONT "   II. ERNEST, born in 1714, who succeeded his brother as eighteenth Baron of Balquhain.
2 CONT
2 CONT "   III. A SON, who died soon after his birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Count George Leslie died 17th June 1715 at Fetternear, aged 34 years, in the vigour of manhood, as appears by an inscription on a stone above the gateway of the old family burying-place at the chapel of Fetternear.  He was succee
2 CONC ded by his eldest son Count James Leslie, seventeenth Baron of Balquhain, then a child four years old.  From this time the ancient splendour of the house of Balquhain began to wane, and the bitterness of anti-Catholic prejudice br
2 CONC ought ruinous consequences on the family, which firmly adhered to the religion of its forefathers."
