1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ROBERT MONTGOMERY OF SKELMORLIE Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 December 1715: Letter from Sir Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie, Bruntisland Castle, to his uncle Hugh Montgomerie of Hartfield, asking forgiveness for having married without latter's knowledge. (Fraser, i, 242). [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f5%2f918&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomerie+of+skelmorlie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Ea
2 CONC rls of Eglinton, reference GD3/5/918]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 Jamuary 1716: Letter from Hugh Montgomerie of Hartfield, Glasgow, to Sir Robert Montgomerie of Skelmorlie: "I can have no further resentment about your marriage". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD3%2f5%2f922&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+montgomerie+of+skelmorlie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/5/922]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Robert Montgomery, Baronet [S 1628], of Skelmorlie</strong>, son and heir; succeeded to the Baronetcy, September 1694; was Gov. of a garrison in Ireland. He married Frances, 1st daughter of Col. Francis Stirling, by A
2 CONC gnes, daughter of Robert Murray, of Blackbarony. He died s.p.m. 15 August 1731, at Limerick. His widow died at Skelmorlie 9 June 1759."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 336
