2 NICK Anne O'Brien 2nd Countess of Orkney
2 NICK Anne Douglas-Hamilton
2 NICK suo jure Countess of Orkney
1 NAME Anne (Hamilton) O'Brien, 2nd Countess of Orkney
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1696
2 ADDR
3 CITY Maidenhead
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1756
1 OCCU Countess Consort of Inchiquin, suo jure Countess of Orkney
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Parents resided in Cliveden House, Taplow, Near Maidenhead (across River boundary) Bucks. Cliveden House was in Buckinghamshire but Maidenhead, the nearest town, was in Berkshire. Photo attached is of Cliveden House.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne O'Brien, Countess of Inchiquin and 2nd Countess of Orkney (born Lady Anne Hamilton; 1696 – 6 December 1756) was a Scottish noblewoman and the eldest daughter of Field Marshal George Hamilton, 1st Earl of Orkney, and his wife,
2 CONC  the former Elizabeth Villiers.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_O%27Brien,_2nd_Countess_of_Orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She became Countess of Inchiquin, through her marriage to her first cousin William O'Brien, 4th Earl of Inchiquin,[1] the O'Brien, Chief of the Name, Prince of Thomond, and Lord of Dál gCais. They were married on 29 March 1720.[2]
2 CONC  Their daughter, Lady Mary (c. 1721–1790), succeeded her mother in the earldom of Orkney.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their other children were:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT # William, Lord O'Brien (1725–1727)
2 CONT # George, Lord O'Brien (born 1728; died in infancy)
2 CONT # Augustus (died in infancy)
2 CONT # Murrough, Viscount Kirkwall (died 1741, in childhood), who was heir to Henry O'Brien, 8th Earl of Thomond, but died before inheriting[3]
2 CONT # Anne (c. 1721–1808)
2 CONT # Frances (died 1740)
2 CONT # Elizabeth (died 1741)
