1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == CAPTAIN WILLIAM MUIRHEAD OF LAUCHOPE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Muirhead: "a  young  gentleman, who went into the army young, was a proper handsome person, rose  soon to a command, but died of his wounds he received at Wynendale." [https://archive.org/details/systemofheraldry02nisb/
2 CONC page/264/mode/1up A System of Heraldry II: 264] It is supposed that Wynedale is [https://military-history.fandom.com/wiki/Battle_of_Wijnendale Wijendale] in which case William Muirhead of Lauchope may have died on or soon after 28
2 CONC  September 1708.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1707: William Muirhead of Laughop. [https://archive.org/details/indexes300scotuoft/page/622/mode/1up Scottish Record Office Indexes., Number 3, Index to the General Register of Sasines, 1701-1720, Lanark, volume 91, folio
2 CONC  195]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 January 1721 x 25 June 1729: Captain William Muirhead of Lauchope. Captain James Muirhead, brother of Captain William Muirhead of Lauchope. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/XIII/114
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 July 1766 x 29 July 1769: Captain William Muirhead of Lauchope. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/XVIII/279]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 October 1772 x 23 November 1778: Captain William Muirhead of Lauchope. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/XX/419]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
