1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James, third titular Duke of Perth</strong>, and but for his father's attainder sixth Earl of Perth, was born 11 May 1713 at Drummond Castle...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...At Culloden he commanded the Macdonald clans on the left of the front line. After that disastrous engagement he escaped with the Prince of Moidart, and from there he sailed along with his brother and other gentlemen on board on
2 CONC e of the French vessels which had been sent there. Worn out, however, by fatigue, and depressed with the unfortunate issue of the campaign, he died during the voyage on 13 May 1746, and was buried at sea...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...The third Duke of Perth having died unmarried, he was succeeded by his brother."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/54/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VII, page 54-55
