1 OCCU Scottish Jacobite and Member of the Parliament of Great Britain
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Hugh Paterson, Baronet [S. 1686], of Bannockburn</strong>, 6. Jan. 1686, presumably s. and h. ; suc. to the Baronetcy in 1696, or 1701, and, as a Baronet, was, in 1708, unduly elected M.P. for Stirlingshire but unseat
2 CONC ed in 1709, being, however, M.P. thereof (three Paris.) 1710-15; Commissioner of Trade [S.], 1711; joined in the Jacobite rising of 1715 and was attainted, whereby the Baronetcy became forfeited in 1716. He entertained Prince Char
2 CONC les Edward at Bannockburn house, 14 Sep. 1745, who made it his headquarters in Jan. 1745/6. He  m. 2 March 1711/2, at Twickenham, Midx., Jean, only da. of Charles (Erskine), Earl of Mar [S.], by Mary, da. of George (Maule), 2d Ear
2 CONC l or Panmure [S.]. She d. 16 Nov. 1763, at Bannockburn. He d., at Touch, 23 March 1777, aged 91 years and 2 months."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n361/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 342
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
