1 NAME Owen /Wynne/ III
2 GIVN Owen
2 NSFX III
2 _MARNM Wynne
1 NAME Captain Owen Wynne, III
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1686
2 PLAC Foxford
2 ADDR
3 CITY Toomore
3 CTRY Ireland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 FEB 1755
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain Owen Wynne was born in 1687 in Foxford, Toomore, Mayo, Ireland. He was the son of Lewis Wynne and Rebecca Bingham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen matriculated at Trinity College, Dublin, Ireland, on 3 February 1703/4
2 CONT
2 CONT As soon as he was able, he served the Crown, aged 19 or 20, by joining the army.  He served as Ensign from 25 Mar 1705. He bought a company two years later and served several years in Flanders. He was placed on the half pay as Lt.
2 CONC  in 1713.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his first cousin, Catherine Ffolliott, daughter of Colonel John Ffolliott of Donegal and his wife Lucy, daughter of Owen Wynne I. Owen III and Catherine had three sons, James, Owen (later Owen IV) and John, and two daug
2 CONC hters, Lucy and Hannah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen  III was High Sheriff of Co. Sligo in 1723 and 1745, he filled the same office in Co. Leitrim in 1724. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1737 He succeeded his uncle [http://www.geni.com/people/Lt-Gen-Owen-Wynne-II/6000000024238659791 Lt. General Owen Wynne II] at Hazelwood in 1737, becoming the first of the Wynne  to combine in one ownership the [http://landedes
2 CONC tates.nuigalway.ie/LandedEstates/jsp/estate-show.jsp?id=51 family lands in Counties Leitrim, Cavan and Sligo].
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Wynne was othe few proprietors of Hazelwood who did not sit in Parliament. Two of his sons, James and Capt. John, between them represented the Borough and County in Parliament for over thirty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Owen Wynne made a will dated 23 May 1755, the year he died, aged 79. His will was proved on 8 July 1756 in the Prerogative Court of Armagh. His wife, Catherine,  died in 1778. Owen III's eldest son, James, died in 1748, ei
2 CONC ght years before his father's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.sligolibrary.ie/sligolibrarynew/media/WYNNES%20(12).pdf\ http://www.linleyfh.com/oursecondsite-p/p937.htm#i11810 http://fernleafields.com/hazelwoodwynnes.htm
