1 NAME Alexander /Murray of Blackbarony/ Baronet
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Murray of Blackbarony
2 NSFX Baronet
2 _MARNM Murray of Blackbarony
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 DEC 1741
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "(339) <strong>Sir Alexander Murray, 4th Baronet of Blackbarony</strong>, died sp. 31st December 1741. Buried Holyrood 30th January 1742. He was M.P. for Peeblesshire 1700-02; and was served heir to his grandfather 3rd January 171
2 CONC 0, and to his father 14th August 1733. He married at Edinburgh, 28th July 1687, Margaret, daughter of William Wallace of Helington. Having no issue, he in 1741 entailed the Blackbarony estate on his niece, Margaret, daughter of Ca
2 CONC ptain Archibald (No. 338, b), and failing her issue, on the Murrays of Elibank (No. 363). He was succeeded in the title by his cousin (No. 341 below)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/n109/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910
2 CONC , page 81, paragraph 339
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n371/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 353
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===SIR ALEXANDER MURRAY OF BLACKBARONY Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/bookofwallace01roge/page/n298 The Book of Wallace I: pp. 133-34]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
