1 NAME George /Ogilvy/ 4th Lord Banff
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Ogilvy
2 NSFX 4th Lord Banff
2 _MARNM Ogilvy
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1670
1 BAPM
2 DATE 4 AUG 1670
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 12 JAN 1718
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George, fourth Lord Banff</strong>, was baptized at Banff 4 August 1670. In 1690, George, third Lord, disponed his lands to his son and heir George, Master of Banff, and a charter under the Great Seal followed 26 February
2 CONC  1697. Succeeded his father in 1713, married, 11 January 1712, Helen, daughter of Sir John Lauder of Fountainhall, Lord of Session. The spouses had a charter under the Great Seal of Inchdrewer, 26 July 1712. He died before 12 Janu
2 CONC ary 1718, and had by Helen Lauder (who was married, secondly, on 27 June 1721, to Alexander Gordon of Glengerrack, and, thirdly, to James Hay, merchant in Banff, second son of James Hay of Rannes, with issue ; she died 22 October 
2 CONC 1742 :
2 CONT * George, baptized 20 February 1714, died in infancy. 
2 CONT * George, baptized 28 November 1715, died in infancy. 
2 CONT * John George, fifth Lord Banff. 
2 CONT * Alexander, sixth Lord Banff."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/20/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. II, page 21
