2 CONT Anne, eldest daughter of Lord Ormiston, married Sir John Inglis, sixth Baronet of Cramond, Postmaster-General for Scotland, who settled upon her by their marriage-contract, dated 24th June 1708, "made with consent of her father, A
2 CONC dam Cockburn of Ormiston, Lord Justice-Clerk, and one of the Senators of the College of Justice," 3000 merks, and 25,000 merks in event of their having children, out of the lands of King's Cramond. Patrick Cockburn of Clerkington,
2 CONC  John Cockburn of Ormiston, Mr. Charles Cockburn, advocate, and John Hepburn of Humbie, were witnesses.
