1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Montgomerie, 9th Earl of Eglinton was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) . He succeeded to the title of 9th Earl of Eglinton in 1701. He succeeded to the title of 10th Lord Montgomerie in 1701. He held
2 CONC  the office of Commissioner of Treasury between 1702 and 1704. He held the office of Representative Peer between 1710 and 1714. 
