1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Montgomerie
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel John Montgomerie (died 1731) was colonial governor of New York and New Jersey from 1728 to 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT Montgomerie was born in the parish of Beith in Scotland and served as Member or Parliament for Ayrshire between 1710 and 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Montgomerie was replaced as governor, on an acting basis, by Rip Van Dam from 1731 to 1732 and then officially by William Cosby.
2 CONT
2 CONT Montgomerie was chosen by King George II of Great Britain for the post.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of an epileptic seizure on 1 July 1731.
