1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1720, apprenticed to William Howard of the Armourers' and Braziers' Company, London. 	
2 CONT
2 CONT London Apprenticeship Abstracts, 1442-1850:
2 CONT
2 CONT Howard Robert, son of Stanley, St Olave Southwark, Surrey, woolstapler, to William Howard, 15 Feb 1720/1, Armourers' and Braziers' Company
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived in Folkestone
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert met Elizabeth, a fisherman's daughter, whilst recovering from burns, He was a tinman and lived in Folkestone in the centre of the town. They were devout quakers .
2 CONT
2 CONT In later life they moved to Wandsworth and after Elizabeth died Robert moved in with his son Thomas at Stockwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Lordsmeade document: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Stanley Howard married Elizabeth Cullen and settled at Folkestone, then a small fishing town and a noted place for smuggling, the facilities of intercourse with the French Coast, and the concealment of the traffic holding o
2 CONC ut inducements to this illicit and demoralizing practice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Elizabeth Howard lived in a house about the centre of town – then as now, very irregular having narrow steep streets in a part of it – and but a mean appearance at the best, though the surrounding fine hills covered wit
2 CONC h verdure and affording pasture for peculiarly handsome flocks of a small race of sheep and the white cliffs with their green summits sloping down to the beach, have always given the old town pleasing environs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Howard’s trade was that of a worker in tin to which were added many goods in brass and iron. The shop was well situated for the retail trade – and the worthy pair thus commencing life were frugal and industrious. A blessing
2 CONC  seemed to attend their honest endeavours – which it is believed has continued to the present day in their successors, those who have walked by the same rule and minded the same thing. Their family consisted of three sons and one 
2 CONC daughter, namely Sarah, Thomas, Robert and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Findmypast
2 CONT
2 CONT Record Transcription: Kent Marriages And Banns
2 CONT
2 CONT First name(s)	Robert Last name	Howard Occupation	Brazier
2 CONT
