1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Douglas, 3rd Marquess of Queensberry, was the second son, and eldest to survive infancy, of James Douglas, 2nd Duke of Queensberry, and his wife, Mary Boyle.  The historical record indicates he was a violent 
2 CONC psychopath.  When he was ten years old he slaughtered a servant, roasting him alive on a spit and had begun to eat the servant before he was discovered.  He was subsequently removed from the succession to his father's titles and p
2 CONC roperties, with the exception of the marquessate of Queensberry.
2 CONT
2 CONT The parish register for Calverley, near Leeds, West Yorkshire, includes the burial record of "James Dowgles, Marquess of Drumlangrick" under the heading "burials at Calverley and Pudsey", but states that he died at "Woodall" and w
2 CONC as buried in "Launsborow" (Londesborough).
