2 CONT Judith left La Rochelle, Aunis, France, in 1651 with MargueriteLeGardeur. Judith was arrested in 1679, and accused of deserting the conjugal homeofher husband, and living with (as husband and wife) Pierre Cavelier.  She was condem
2 CONC ned to 10 years ofbannishment on the Isle of Montreal.
2 CONT
