2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors Jean and Pierre Terrien
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors, Pierre and Gabrielle, Jean and Judith
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre Terrien and Gabrielle Mignot
2 CONT
2 CONT April 5, 1656 front the Moreau notary of LaRochelle, Pierre begins to work in Quebec for one three years period with wages of 60 livres per annum (roughly 40,00$) all paid expenditure. After this period, Pierre decides to be estab
2 CONC lished on the Island of Orleans. May 17, 1670 he marries Gabrielle Minau and from this couple were born 12 boys and two girls.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage certificate of Jean Terrien and Judith Rigaud
2 CONT
2 CONT The year of grace 1667, the twenty-sixth day of January, after the proclammation of the bans made by three consecutive Sundays, the first the 9th second 16th, the last 2é the day of the known as month, in the parochial mass; being
2 CONC  found any prevention canonical, me, Jean Frémont, priest of this parish of the Three-Rivers, day questioned Jean Terrien in the church of this parish, son of Jean Terrien and Marie Hélie, her father and mother, of the parish of S
2 CONC t-Jacques de Dieppe, and Judith Rigault, this same parish, widow of François LeMaistre, inhabitant of this place; and, having received their mutual assent, the married day, with the required ceremonies, in the presence of Maurice 
2 CONC Foal and of Louis Godefroy known as Normandville.
