1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis Armand I de Bourbon, Prince de Conti (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #220214, b. 4 April 1661, d. 9 October 1685
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=3 Oct 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Armand I de Bourbon, Prince de Conti was born on 4 April 1661 at Paris, France. (1) He was the son of Armand de Bourbon, Prince de Conti and Anne Marie Martinozzi. (1) He married Marie Anne de Bourbon, daughter of Louis XIV,
2 CONC  Roi de France and Louise Françoise de la Baume le Blanc, Duchesse de la Vallière, on 16 January 1680 at Saint-Germain-en-Laye, Île-de-France, France. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 9 October 1685 at age 24 at Fontainebleau, Île-de-France, France. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Louis Armand I de Bourbon, Prince de Conti gained the title of Prince de Conti. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p22022.htm#i220214
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Anne de Bourbon
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1685, her husband contracted smallpox from Marie Anne. Although she recovered, he succumbed after five days. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Anne_de_Bourbon
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Armand I, Prince of Conti
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Armand I de Bourbon (1661–1685) was Prince of Conti from 1666 to his death, succeeding his father, Armand de Bourbon. As a member of the reigning House of Bourbon, he was a Prince du Sang.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Armand was born in Paris. In 1680 he married Marie Anne de Bourbon, the illegitimate daughter of King Louis XIV and his first mistress, Louise de la Vallière. The bride and groom were respectively thirteen and fifteen years 
2 CONC old at the time. Since neither of them had been instructed on what to expect on their first night together, it ended up in disaster with the young princess fleeing in despair and the prince not wanting to share the bed of a woman 
2 CONC again.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served with distinction in Flanders in 1683, and, against the wish of the king, went to Hungary, where he helped the Imperialists defeat the Turks at Gran in the same year. He died in Fontainebleau from smallpox which he contra
2 CONC cted from his wife. While she recovered after some time, the prince succumbed after five days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Having no descendants, he was succeeded as Prince of Conti by his younger brother, François Louis de Bourbon (1664–1709).
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Armand_I,_Prince_of_Conti
