1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch====
2 CONT * Wikipedia - English - [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_de_Noailles_%281715%E2%80%931794%29 '''Philippe de Noailles....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe de Noailles, comte de Noailles and later prince de Poix, duc de Mouchy, and duc de Poix à brevêt (27 December 1715 in Paris – 27 June 1794 in Paris), was a younger brother of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_de_Noaille
2 CONC s '''Louis de Noailles'''], and a more distinguished soldier than his brother. He was the son of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7oise_Charlotte_d%27Aubign%C3%A9 '''Françoise Charlotte d'Aubigné'''], niece of Madame de Main
2 CONC tenon.
2 CONT ====Life====
2 CONT He served at Minden and in other campaigns, and was made a marshal of France in 1775, on the same day as his brother. He was long in great favor at court, and his wife, Anne d'Arpajon, comtesse de Noailles, was first lady of honor
2 CONC  to [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Antoinette '''Marie Antoinette'''], and was nicknamed by her Madame Etiquette. This court favor brought down punishment in the days of the French Revolution, and the old marshal, his sister,
2 CONC  his wife, daughter-in-law and granddaughter were all [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillotine '''guillotined'''] on 27 June 1794. Twenty-five days later, the widow, daughter-in-law, and granddaughter of the 4th duc de Noailles we
2 CONC re guillotined.
2 CONT
2 CONT The comte de Noailles received the Spanish title of prince de Poix in 1729, and that of duc de Mouchy in 1747. In 1767 he received the additional French title of duc de Poix à brevêt. The title of prince de Poix passed to his son 
2 CONC Charles-Adrien as a courtesy title on the latter's birth in 1747, and after the child's death later that year and the infant deaths of two further sons, came to rest on Noailles's successor, Philippe-Louis-Marc-Antoine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two of de Noailles's three surviving sons, Philippe-Louis-Marc-Antoine and Louis-Marie, were members of the National Constituent Assembly; Louis-Marie's wife died with his parents.
2 CONT (car)
