1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:B4QkJbW6JcYJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Louise_%C3%89lisabeth_d%27Orl%C3%A9ans+&cd=1&hl=en&ct=clnk&lr= en.wikipedia.org...] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Louise Élisabeth d'Orléans (20 August 1695 – 21 July 1719) was a member of the House of Orléans who married Charles, Duke of Berry, youngest grandson of Louis XIV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Louise Élisabeth d'Orléans was born at the Palace of Versailles. She was the eldest of the surviving children of Philippe II, Duke of Orléans, Regent of France, and of his wife Françoise Marie de Bourbon, a legitimised daugh
2 CONC ter of Louis XIV of France. She was given the honorary title of Mademoiselle d'Orléans at birth. After her marriage the title would be given to her younger sister Louise Adélaïde d'Orléans. She was baptised at Saint-Cloud on 29 Ju
2 CONC ly 1696.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Élisabeth grew up at the Palais-Royal, the Orléans residence in Paris. After recovering from a near fatal illness at the age of six, her father personally nursed her day and night in order to save her life.[2] Her paternal 
2 CONC grandmother, Elizabeth Charlotte of the Palatinate, Madame, known since her childhood as Liselotte, wrote in her memoirs that from a very early age, Louise Élisabeth: ... had entirely her own way, so that it is not surprising she 
2 CONC should be like a headstrong horse.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of ten, Louise Élisabeth, again caught smallpox at Saint-Cloud and her grandmother wrote in her memoirs that Mademoiselle d'Orléans was presumed dead for over six hours.[3] - [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/searc
2 CONC h?q=cache:B4QkJbW6JcYJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Louise_%C3%89lisabeth_d%27Orl%C3%A9ans+&cd=1&hl=en&ct=clnk&lr=  '''read more...''']
