1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for PENNSYLVANIA with the rank of CAPTAIN.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A032121  DAR Ancestor #  A032121]
2 CONT
2 CONT His ancestor was Isaac DeTurk, a French Huguenot, who fled to the Palatinate of Germany, emigrated to Esopus, New York, and from thence, to Oley township of berks County, between 1704 and 1712. It was in a barn of this family, in 
2 CONC Oley township, that the first Indian converts of the Moravians were babtized. He was commissioned a Captain of the Flying Camp, and, with his company, passed through Bethlehem, August 26, 1776, on his way to the front.
2 CONT  DAR Ancestor #: A032121
