1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/15665875/person/112060301621 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 2 2021, 3:09:32 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT His tombstone also says son of Jacob Hummel and gives his age at death 71y, 6m, 6d.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick was the youngest son of John Jacob Hummel and Eva Marie DeTurk of Berks County, PA.  He and his brother John Jacob, buried in the same cemetery, came to the Hummels Wharf area in the 1790's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A deed recorded in 1847 says that Frederick Hummel died intestate and Michael Hummel is now buying Frederick's land from Frederick’s other heirs:  Jacob F and wife Margaret, Samuel, John and wife Susannah, John St Clair and Elizab
2 CONC eth his wife, Henry Sheets and Sarah Ann his wife and Edward and the heirs of Benjamin.  Some of the land had been acquired by Frederick from Jacob Becker in 1804.  Benjamin’s heirs were:  Benjamin, Elizabeth, John and Catherine.*
2 CONC  Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/150401044/john-frederick-hummel Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 1 2022, 0:53:43 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT His tombstone clearly says Johannes Friederich, rather than Johann Friederich which was likely how he was baptized.  But, like most German boys with the first name Johann, he went through life known by his middle name, Frederick. 
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT His tombstone also says son of Jacob Hummel and gives his age at death 71y, 6m, 6d.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick was the youngest son of John Jacob Hummel and Eva Marie DeTurk of Berks County, PA.  He and his brother John Jacob, buried in the same cemetery, came to the Hummels Wharf area in the 1790's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A deed recorded in 1847 says that Frederick Hummel died intestate and Michael Hummel is now buying Frederick's land from Frederick's other heirs:  Jacob F and wife Margaret, Samuel, John and wife Susannah, John St Clair and Elizab
2 CONC eth his wife, Henry Sheets and Sarah Ann his wife and Edward and the heirs of Benjamin.  Some of the land had been acquired by Frederick from Jacob Becker in 1804.  Benjamin's heirs were:  Benjamin, Elizabeth, John and Catherine.*
2 CONC  Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/150401044/johannes_friederich_hummel Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 4 2024, 13:55:28 UTC''
