1 NOTE    Susan de Benneville died Sunday Jan 15,1837 at age 88 yrs 8 mo.  She was
2 CONT    the second child of Dr George de Benneville, was born in Oley Twp. May 15
2 CONT    1748. She later moved with her parents to Bristol Twp Phila Co. where she
2 CONT    married John Keim of Reading which later became her residence.  She went
2 CONT    to the retreat of Anna Maria Young, the recluse of the Oley mountains,
2 CONT    (a few days before her death) where she died. [Reading Historical Socity]
2 CONT MARRIED: Married to John Keim the 15 day of October 1771 by Jacob Hall
2 CONT          Justice of the Peace in and for the County of Phila.
2 CONT          [Keim and Allied Families page 81]
2 CONT BURIED:  First buried, on the present farm of Wm. Cleaver, at Lime Kiln,Pa.
2 CONT          and in 1847 reburied in lots at Charles Evans Cemetery by his son
2 CONT          Benneville Keim. [Oley Valley Graveyard Ramblings by Chester Deturk
2 CONT          and Laurel Miller] and [Charles Evans Cemetery Records]
2 CONT    Chirst Episcopal Church Records 1825-1919 indexed by Mrs Mary O Steinmetz
1 CHAN
2 DATE 14 NOV 2024
3 TIME 10:32:19
