1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncan_Forbes_of_Culloden_%28judge,_born_1685%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan Forbes, 5th of Culloden (10 November 1685 – 10 December 1747) was a Scottish lawyer and Whig politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1721 to 1737. As Lord President and senior Scottish legal officer, he played a maj
2 CONC or role in helping the government suppress the 1745 Jacobite Rising.
2 CONT
2 CONT He returned home in 1707 and in October 1708 married '''Mary Rose (1690-before 1717'''), daughter of Hugh Rose, 15th of Kilravock, whose family owned nearby Kilravock Castle. Forbes inherited the Culloden estates when his elder br
2 CONC other died childless in 1734 and these later passed to his son John (1710-1772).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p56209.htm#i562090
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Rose is the daughter of Hugh Rose, 15th of Kilravock and Margaret Campbell.2 She married Duncan Forbes, 5th of Culloden, son of Duncan Forbes, 3rd of Culloden and Marie Innes, on 21 October 1708.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Rose and Duncan Forbes, 5th of Culloden
2 CONT
2 CONT #Elizabeth Forbes+3 (mother is not confirmed) 
2 CONT # John Forbes, 6th of Culloden+4 b. c 1710, d. 26 Sep 1772
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Rose%2C_15th_of_Kilravock
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Rose, 15th Baron of Kilravock and Chief of Clan Rose, (1663–1732) was one of the Scottish representatives to the first Parliament of Great Britain as MP for Nairnshire.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rose married, firstly, Margaret Campbell, daughter of Sir Hugh Campbell, 5th of Cawdor and Lady Henrietta Stuart, daughter of James Stuart, 4th Earl of Moray, on 19 October 1683, they had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hugh Rose, 16th of Kilravock (died 1755), MP for Ross-shire.
2 CONT # Margaret Rose (died 1703), married Sir John Mackenzie of Coul, 3rd Baronet, had issue.
2 CONT # Mary Rose (died 1734) [sic: before 1717], married Duncan Forbes, 5th of Culloden, had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT page 382 of ‘’The Family of Rose’’: < [https://books.google.com/books?id=rb9GCo3_bqYC&pg=PA382&lpg=PA382&dq=elizabeth+calder+rose+hugh+rose&source=bl&ots=byyVeDyTYY&sig=1FRBsUcK2e-cSvhzri7ON7nFPBk&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CC4Q6AEwA2oVChMI9
2 CONC v-D8YulyAIVSC2ICh1WzwKL#v=onepage&q=elizabeth%20calder%20rose%20hugh%20rose&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
2 CONT >‘’ His [Hugh Rose, 15th of Kilravock] first Lady was '''Margaret Campbell''', eldest daughter of Sir Hugh Campbell of Calder and Lady Henriette Stuart, daughter of James Earl of Muray and of Lady Margaret Home, daughter of the Ea
2 CONC rl of Home. Kilravock married this Lady on the 19th of October 1683, and she died in the year ….. having brought him a son, Hugh, and two daughters, viz., Margaret, married to Sir John Mackenzie of Coul, and Mary, married to Mr. D
2 CONC uncan Forbes, Advocate, (and afterwards Lord Advo- cate, President of the College of Justice, and Laird of Culloden,) to whom she bore John Forbes now of Culloden.’’
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
