1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the same as her younger 1/2 sister, https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Rose/6000000204341410828?through=6000000015918542496
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Rose''' (d c1703) was the elder daughter of Hugh Rose, 15th of Kilravock, Sheriff of Ross (b 01.1663, d 23.01.1732 and his first wife,  (19.10.1683) Margaret Campbell (dau of Sir Hugh Campbell, 5th of Cawdor).  
2 CONT
2 CONT She married as his first wife, on 04 February 1701, to Sir John Mackenzie, 3rd Bart of Coul.  He was the son of Sir Alexander Mackenzie, 2nd Bart of Coul (d 1702) & Jean Gordon (dau of Sir Robert Gordon of Gordonstoun).
2 CONT
2 CONT Their child was 
2 CONT # 	a.	(Jean?) Mackenzie  	m. (Robert) Bayne of Delny (d 1743)
2 CONT
2 CONT She died before 1703, when he married Helen Murray.  She had a younger 1/2 sister also called Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir John Mackenzie, Baronet [S. 1673], of Coul, 1st s. and h. by 1st wife, b. in or before 1673 ; suc. to the 1715. Baronetcy in 1702; joined in the rising of 1715, and, not having rendered himself up to justice before 30 June 17
2 CONC 16, was attainted, under the Act, 13 Nov, 1715. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. firstly, '''Margaret, da. of Hugh Rose, of Kilravock.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. secondly, in 1703, Helen (b. 27 Feb. 1683), 4th da. of Patrick (Murray), 3d Lord Elibank [S.], by Anne, da. of Alexander Burnet, Archbishop of St. Andrew's. He d. s.p.m. soon after 1715, the Baronetcy, by his abovementioned 
2 CONC attainder in that year, having previously become forfeited."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n315/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 297
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
