1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY EMILIA STUART Countess of Crawford ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Dame Emillia Stuart (1705) Emilia Stewart (1706) Emilia Stewart (1707) Ellizabeth, Countess of Crawford (1711)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT A date and place of birth has not been identified for Lady Emilia Stuart, here treated, but she was probably born between 26 December 1677, the date upon which her parents were contracted to marry, and the year 1685, when her fath
2 CONC er is reported to have died.  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 323]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Emilia Stuart died on 18 February 1711. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Amelia Stuart was buried on 26 February 1711, in the Abbey of Holyrood House, in the Canongate near Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso14scotuoft/page/5/mode/1up Holyroodhouse Bur
2 CONC ials: 5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Burial Records of the Holyrood Burial Register ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1711: Elizabeth (sic), Countess of Crawford, was buried in the Abbay Church of Holyroodhouse, on the north side of the church, and east end, betwixt the eastmost whole pillar and half pillar thereof, to the south si
2 CONC de of the foresaid pillars. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso14scotuoft/page/5/mode/1up Register of Burials in the Chapel Royal or Abbey of Holyroodhouse, 1706-1900. (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1900), p. 5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Emilia Stuart married,  Alexander Fraser of Strichen, [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Emilia Stuart married John, nineteenth Earl of Crawford. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "<strong>Emilia</strong>, married first, to Alexander Fraser of Strichen, and, secondly, to John, nineteenth Earl of Crawfurd. She died age of 32, and was buried at Holyrood 26, February 1711."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/322/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 323
2 CONT >SOURCE [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2336.htm#i23356 Darryl Lundy's Peerage: The Peerage, person page 2336]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2125.htm#i21243
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Emilia Stuart was the daughter of James Stuart, Lord Doune and Catherine Tollemache.1,2 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Alexander Fraser, 5th of Strichen, son of Thomas Fraser, 4th of Strichen and Marion Irvine, in 1697.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Lt.-Gen. John Lindsay, 19th Earl of Crawford, son of William Lindsay, 18th Earl of Crawford and Lady Mary Johnstone, before 1702.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 18 February 1711.1 She was buried on 21 February 1711 at Holyrood Church, Edinburgh, Midlothian, ScotlandG.1
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1697, her married name became Fraser.1 From before 1702, her married name became Lindsay.1 After her marriage, Hon. Emilia Stuart was styled as Countess of Crawford before 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hon. Emilia Stuart and Alexander Fraser, 5th of Strichen
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Fraser, 6th of Strichen3
2 CONT # Alexander Fraser, Lord Strichen+3 d. 15 Feb 1775
2 CONT # Marian Fraser3
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hon. Emilia Stuart and Lt.-Gen. John Lindsay, 19th Earl of Crawford
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lady Catherine Lindsay3 b. 14 Feb 1697
2 CONT # Lt.-Gen. John Lindsay, 20th Earl of Crawford1 b. 4 Oct 1702, d. 25 Dec 1749.  “ At Belford on 3 March 1747 he married Lady Jean Murray but she died of fever within six months. He himself died on 24 December 1749 in great sufferi
2 CONC ng from a wound, inflicted in 1739, which had broken out for the 29th time.”
2 CONT # Captain William Lindsay+3 b. 3 Apr 1705
2 CONT # Lady Mary Lindsay+3 b. 24 Sep 1706
2 CONT
2 CONT
