1 NOTE {geni:about_me} " Alexander Gordon, Lord Rockville (1739 – 13 March 1792) was a Scottish judge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rockville was the youngest son of William Gordon, 2nd Earl of Aberdeen, by his third wife Lady Anne, daughter of Alexander Gordon, 2nd Duke of Gordon. He served as a Lord of Session from 1788 to 1792 under the judicial title Lord 
2 CONC Rockville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rockville married Anne, daughter of William Duff and widow of William Dalrymple-Crichton, 5th Earl of Dumfries, in 1769. One of their sons was Sir William Duff-Gordon, 2nd Baronet. He died in March 1792. Lady Rockville died in 181
2 CONC 1."
